@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+# dublin_board.dem — v2-dublin-board's named golden (stage 1 of the real-maps
+# arc): the Dublin cross-section board (data/maps/dublin.json, merged in #90)
+# under the growth director — the board REPLACES the procedural terrain, and
+# growth spawns land on the board's real-street tile pool (the 1-in-6 density,
+# the user's blessed calm default) with estates clustering within districts
+# (the growth_groups interplay: the ATTACH family draws from the anchor's
+# district pool — a cluster never crosses a district boundary).
+#
+# The mesh: two high routers on the city core's street tiles ((20,15) + (16,12)
+# are pool tiles near Temple Bar / the Liffey) joined by a wide fiber — the
+# era-3 connect span (18) + the dense core give the growth director the
+# widest valid spawn surface. Spawns are seed-derived (the 5.1 canon): the
+# T1 manifest pins the full timeline; the T2 captures show the board underlay
+# + the grown terminals + the player-built wire.
+#
+# T1 pins (replay gate + manifest): every per-tick hash incl. the growth
+# spawns (replay byte-identical [E10] — the replay re-derives the same
+# spawns from the same seed + the same board bytes).
+seed 2026
+era 3
+run 90000ms
+fixture off
+map dublin
+growth on
+spawn_node router_high 20 15
+spawn_node router_high 16 12
+at 100ms draw 0 1 wide
+capture at 30000ms
+capture at 90000ms
